{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43340766",
      "title": "Setting Up A Form Action",
      "lectureOrder": 167,
      "videoOrder": 155,
      "sourceHash": "a16752c44417627a20b6200c7762ef548102f4de043d730101ea8aa238d5def2",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.78,
          "end": 3.84,
          "en": "So what are Server Actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.84,
          "end": 7.38,
          "en": "and how can we use this Server Actions concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.38,
          "end": 11.19,
          "en": "to handle data submissions with NextJS?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.19,
          "end": 14.85,
          "en": "Well, first, it's important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.85,
          "end": 16.74,
          "en": "that Server Actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.74,
          "end": 21.06,
          "en": "are actually not a NextJS-specific feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.06,
          "end": 25.14,
          "en": "but actually a feature that is supported by React itself",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.14,
          "end": 28.56,
          "en": "if you're using React in an environment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.56,
          "end": 30.39,
          "en": "where this feature works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.39,
          "end": 35.34,
          "en": "which is not the case in your standard React project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.34,
          "end": 39.24,
          "en": "which might be a pure client-side React project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.24,
          "end": 43.26,
          "en": "but which in the end can be unlocked by frameworks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.26,
          "end": 47.013,
          "en": "like NextJS that wrap around React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 47.97,
          "end": 49.53,
          "en": "So this React feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.53,
          "end": 51.78,
          "en": "this Server Actions React feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.78,
          "end": 56.46,
          "en": "is in the end, unlocked by frameworks like NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.46,
          "end": 60.27,
          "en": "Still, it is a feature built directly into React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 60.27,
          "end": 63,
          "en": "that's then made available by NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 63,
          "end": 64.98,
          "en": "to put it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.98,
          "end": 68.49,
          "en": "But what's the idea behind Server Actions?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.49,
          "end": 70.62,
          "en": "Well, let's create an action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.62,
          "end": 74.37,
          "en": "and let's handle the submission of this form here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.37,
          "end": 76.95,
          "en": "which you find in the new-post folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.95,
          "end": 78.51,
          "en": "in the app folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.51,
          "end": 80.97,
          "en": "in that page.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.97,
          "end": 83.34,
          "en": "Let's handle the submission of this form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.34,
          "end": 84.93,
          "en": "with a Server Action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.93,
          "end": 89.76,
          "en": "and along the way learn what a Server Action is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.76,
          "end": 92.00999999999999,
          "en": "So to handle the submission of this form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.00999999999999,
          "end": 95.1,
          "en": "with a Server Action, I'll actually start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.1,
          "end": 98.7,
          "en": "by handling the submission with a non-Server Action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.7,
          "end": 102.27000000000001,
          "en": "with just a form action instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.27000000000001,
          "end": 104.67,
          "en": "And that's another feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.67,
          "end": 107.94,
          "en": "built into React itself already",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.94,
          "end": 110.00999999999999,
          "en": "though at least at the point of time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.00999999999999,
          "end": 112.95,
          "en": "where I'm recording this video, it's not stable yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.95,
          "end": 115.74000000000001,
          "en": "but it will eventually be a stable feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.74000000000001,
          "end": 120.15,
          "en": "that can also be used in client-side React applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.15,
          "end": 122.64,
          "en": "So in all React projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.64,
          "end": 126.57,
          "en": "even if you're not using a framework like NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.57,
          "end": 127.86,
          "en": "because there is a difference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.86,
          "end": 132.36,
          "en": "between a form action and a Server Action as you will see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.36,
          "end": 135.27,
          "en": "And the idea in the end simply is that React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 135.27,
          "end": 137.49,
          "en": "gives you a way of handling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.49,
          "end": 141.93,
          "en": "form submissions on the client or server-side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 141.93,
          "end": 144.66,
          "en": "in an easier and simpler way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.66,
          "end": 147.36,
          "en": "than it used to be in the past.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.36,
          "end": 152.36,
          "en": "And a form action simply is a function you define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.73,
          "end": 156.42000000000002,
          "en": "either directly in the component like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.42000000000002,
          "end": 159.75,
          "en": "or in a separate file that doesn't matter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 159.75,
          "end": 163.65,
          "en": "and you can give this function any name of your choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 163.65,
          "end": 167.49,
          "en": "For example, createPost could be a fitting name here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 167.49,
          "end": 171,
          "en": "and you then pass this function, which we created here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 171,
          "end": 173.76,
          "en": "You pass that as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 173.76,
          "end": 178.07999999999998,
          "en": "to the action prop on the form element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 178.07999999999998,
          "end": 179.7,
          "en": "and that's new.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 179.7,
          "end": 184.7,
          "en": "This action prop is actually a default attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 184.92,
          "end": 187.11,
          "en": "you can set on the form element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 187.11,
          "end": 189.18,
          "en": "even if you're not using React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 189.18,
          "end": 191.01,
          "en": "But when using React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 191.01,
          "end": 194.31,
          "en": "React takes over that prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 194.31,
          "end": 196.26,
          "en": "and that attribute, so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 196.26,
          "end": 198.99,
          "en": "and handles it slightly differently",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 198.99,
          "end": 201.09,
          "en": "than it would normally work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 201.09,
          "end": 204,
          "en": "Because normally on the form element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 204,
          "end": 207.15,
          "en": "if you are not using React or a React version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 207.15,
          "end": 210.75,
          "en": "that doesn't support that form actions feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 210.75,
          "end": 212.82,
          "en": "the action attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 212.82,
          "end": 216.18,
          "en": "that can be set on a form element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 216.18,
          "end": 219.81,
          "en": "in the end, defines the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 219.81,
          "end": 223.8,
          "en": "to which the browser will automatically send a request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 223.8,
          "end": 225.663,
          "en": "once the form is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 226.77,
          "end": 230.67000000000002,
          "en": "So that's a default behavior built into the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 230.67000000000002,
          "end": 233.37,
          "en": "This action prop or attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 233.37,
          "end": 235.95,
          "en": "normally defines the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 235.95,
          "end": 239.04,
          "en": "to which the form data will be automatically submitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 239.04,
          "end": 242.25,
          "en": "once you press a submit button inside of the form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 242.25,
          "end": 246.21,
          "en": "That's what this action prop normally does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 246.21,
          "end": 249.9,
          "en": "Now when using a React version that supports form actions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 249.9,
          "end": 252.24,
          "en": "or NextJS as we do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 252.24,
          "end": 255.93,
          "en": "this action prop will work slightly differently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 255.93,
          "end": 260.13,
          "en": "Instead of accepting a URL, it will accept a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 260.13,
          "end": 264.3,
          "en": "and React will prevent that browser default behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 264.3,
          "end": 267.33,
          "en": "of sending a request to some URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 267.33,
          "end": 269.79,
          "en": "and instead trigger that function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 269.79,
          "end": 271.323,
          "en": "when the form is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 272.76,
          "end": 275.31,
          "en": "And conveniently, it will then give you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 275.31,
          "end": 277.62,
          "en": "a formData object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 277.62,
          "end": 279.81,
          "en": "which it will pass into this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 279.81,
          "end": 282.65999999999997,
          "en": "as an argument automatically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 282.65999999999997,
          "end": 285.6,
          "en": "which allows you to extract the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 285.6,
          "end": 288.12,
          "en": "that was entered into the different inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 288.12,
          "end": 289.203,
          "en": "of that form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 290.25,
          "end": 292.23,
          "en": "And that formData object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 292.23,
          "end": 294.75,
          "en": "is based on that formData interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 294.75,
          "end": 298.47,
          "en": "which is also a standard thing in the web,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 298.47,
          "end": 301.56,
          "en": "not React-specific, which in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 301.56,
          "end": 304.95,
          "en": "defines an object that contains various methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 304.95,
          "end": 308.31,
          "en": "like this get method that you can use to extract",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 308.31,
          "end": 311.82,
          "en": "the data that was entered by the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 311.82,
          "end": 313.95,
          "en": "So we can use this formData object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 313.95,
          "end": 316.98,
          "en": "which we get automatically here to call the get method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 316.98,
          "end": 319.5,
          "en": "to get hold of the different input values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 319.5,
          "end": 321.18,
          "en": "entered by the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 321.18,
          "end": 324.48,
          "en": "And we do get hold of these different values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 324.48,
          "end": 327.33,
          "en": "with help of the name prop and attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 327.33,
          "end": 330.27,
          "en": "that's set on those elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 330.27,
          "end": 333.12,
          "en": "and that's therefore all important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 333.12,
          "end": 337.08,
          "en": "When using such a form action as we're doing it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 337.08,
          "end": 338.73,
          "en": "and that's all important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 338.73,
          "end": 340.83,
          "en": "this is not a Server Action yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 340.83,
          "end": 342.18,
          "en": "It's a form action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 342.18,
          "end": 345.09000000000003,
          "en": "but it will soon become a Server Action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 345.09000000000003,
          "end": 347.37,
          "en": "When you're using such a form action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 347.37,
          "end": 350.73,
          "en": "you must set these name attributes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 350.73,
          "end": 352.5,
          "en": "on all the inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 352.5,
          "end": 355.56,
          "en": "of which you want to extract their values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 355.56,
          "end": 357.93,
          "en": "because it will be those name values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 357.93,
          "end": 360.21,
          "en": "that you now use with the get method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 360.21,
          "end": 362.82,
          "en": "like here, get('title') to extract",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 362.82,
          "end": 365.43,
          "en": "that inputs value here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 365.43,
          "end": 368.313,
          "en": "to get hold of any values entered by the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 369.33,
          "end": 373.53,
          "en": "So that would give me the title value entered by the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 373.53,
          "end": 375.09,
          "en": "And we can now repeat that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 375.09,
          "end": 377.34,
          "en": "to all to get hold of the image file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 377.34,
          "end": 379.227,
          "en": "with help of formData.get('image').",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 380.16,
          "end": 384.45,
          "en": "And yes, it does work with file pickers just like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 384.45,
          "end": 387.09,
          "en": "You can also extract those files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 387.09,
          "end": 389.34,
          "en": "And soon, I'll also show you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 389.34,
          "end": 392.82,
          "en": "how to then upload and store them in a safe way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 392.82,
          "end": 396.96,
          "en": "And we can get hold of the content that was entered here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 396.96,
          "end": 399.09000000000003,
          "en": "with help of that content name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 399.09000000000003,
          "end": 401.043,
          "en": "which is set on that text area.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 401.90999999999997,
          "end": 406.563,
          "en": "So with formData.get('content') like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 408.33,
          "end": 409.89,
          "en": "And now here for the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 409.89,
